;; ============================================================
;; src/main.watx — THE source manifest for Wine-Assembly.
;;
;; This file is the ONE hand-maintained source order (Milestone 2.1 of
;; docs/watx-migration-plan.md). Everything else that needs the order derives
;; from it or is gated against it:
;;
;;   - lib/compile-wat.js  WAT_FILES  — the legacy compiler's list. It is
;;     VERIFIED against this file by tools/check-wat-manifest.js, which runs
;;     first in tools/build.sh. Editing one without the other fails the build.
;;   - tools/concat-wat.js — writes build/combined.wat from WAT_FILES, adding
;;     the outer (module ...) wrapper that no source fragment carries.
;;
;; TO ADD OR REORDER A PART: edit the include list HERE first, then mirror it
;; into WAT_FILES. Filename order (LC_ALL=C sort) is also enforced.
;;
;; Include paths are relative to src/ — the same strings WAT_FILES holds — so a
;; driver populates the compiler's vfs by reading src/<name> for each key.
;;
;; No fragment below contains a (module ...) wrapper: each balances its own
;; parentheses (gated by tools/check-wat-fragments.js), which is what lets the
;; WATX compiler's include resolver splice them as top-level module fields and
;; what lets lib/compile-wat.js parse each part independently.
;; ============================================================
